          equipment: '1-2 standard decks with jokers, score sheet',
          dealing: '10 cards dealt to each player. Remaining cards form stock. No discard pile in this game.',
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Get rid of cards by melding. Knock when hand totals â‰¤5 points to end round. Lowest hand wins round. First to 150+ points ends game and scores bonuses.',
          gameplay: "Turn: Must draw 1st card, then either meld OR draw 2nd card. If drew 2nd, must either meld OR draw 3rd card. If drew 3rd card, cannot meld this turn. No discard pile - only draw and meld. Melds: sequences (3+ same suit, Ace high or low not both) or groups (3+ same rank, different suits). Jokers wild. Key feature: Can rearrange ALL table melds when melding, breaking up existing sets and reforming them, provided you add at least one new card from hand and all table cards end in valid melds. Joker value fixed when played, can be moved if released by substituting actual card it represents. Released joker must be used immediately in new meld, cannot return to hand. Knock: After melding with â‰¤5 points in hand, can knock to end round. No layoffs. Winner has lowest hand. Scoring: Winner scores differences from other players' hands. If winner is not knocker, gets 10-point undercut bonus. Going out completely: 25 bonus. Game to 150: winner gets 100 bonus, all get 25 per hand won.",
          keyRules: [
            'Draw 1-3 cards per turn; must meld after 1 or 2 draws',
            'Cannot meld after drawing 3rd card',
            'No discard pile',
            'Can rearrange ALL table melds when playing',
            'Must add at least one new card from hand when melding',
            'Sequences: 3+ same suit, Ace high or low (not both)',
            'Groups: 3+ same rank, different suits',
            'Jokers wild, value fixed when played',
            'Released joker must be used immediately',
            'Knock with â‰¤5 points to end round',
            'No layoffs after knock',
            "Undercut bonus if winner didn't knock",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Focus on reducing hand value. Meld early to get cards out, but remember that table melds help opponents manipulate. Knock when you have a low hand.',
          intermediate: 'Track which cards have been played to estimate what opponents hold. Plan manipulation moves in advance - visualize how you can rearrange table melds before your turn. Use jokers strategically.',
          advanced: 'Control the pace by deciding when to meld. Sometimes holding cards is better than helping opponents with table melds. Complex manipulation chains can empty your hand in one turn. Knock timing is crucial - too early and someone might undercut; too late and opponent may go out completely.',
          tips: [
            'Hoarding cards is common - everyone waits for others to meld first',
            'Jokers are powerful but worth 25 points if stuck in hand',
            'Look for manipulation opportunities that use multiple cards from your hand',
            'Knocking with exactly 5 is risky - others may have less',
            'Going out completely for 25 bonus is often worth the risk',
            "Track high cards - they're worth the most stuck in hands",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
